  "design": {
    "decision": "Once the contract is safe, duck instead of overtaking: give opponents the overtricks, bid low, and let partner's nil cover come from the opponents. The points are lost on a set, so bidding too low to be safe still fails.",
    "opponent": "Revealed on the first trick the opponents win. Opponents may refuse tricks too, which risks their own contract, or push the team toward a set by ducking and forcing it to win.",
    "rationale": "The brief asks for one more decision-rich Exact or Nil–Exact piece. The kept pool's Exact pieces are all result triggers, and every growth and nil-points Exact variant failed badly (for example ub-exact-nil-points at −12.3). This piece turns every trick after the contract is safe into a choice to duck or overtake, the core Exact skill, without another 'makes exactly' clause. It is the points version of the kept rare rb-opp-win-mult, at uncommon strength. Because it is points, it pays only on a made contract, which keeps bids tense.",
